                                                                        <tr>
                                                                            <th>Brief Profile:</th>
                                                                            <td><p align="justify">Prof. (Dr.) Shikha Rai has two decades of experience in teaching and research. Her areas include communication theories, cultural studies, communication management, media marketing, social media, OTT and online learning. A university merit holder at the graduate and post-graduate level, she was also a gold medalist in Post Graduate Diploma in Distance Education (PGDDE) of IGNOU. She was awarded the Commonwealth of Learning (COL) fellowship for the Post Graduate Diploma in E-Learning (PGDEL). She has published over 30 research papers in indexed journals. She is researching social and behavioural change communication in tribal areas during the pandemic, social media outrage, political communication on social media through satire and parody and cultural representation in animation. She is the co-PI of an ICSSR-funded major project titled ‘Youth Engagement and Social Networking Platforms: Assessing the Impact of COVID-19 and Future Challenges in North-East India’.</p>
<p align="justify">Her work at IGNOU comprises teaching and coordinating the Ph.D. programme, MA programme in Journalism and Mass Communication, MAJMC Online, BA programme in Journalism and Digital Media, and Postgraduate Diploma in Journalism and Mass Communication. The Diploma and Master’s programmes are offered in 16 African countries, besides India, through the Ministry of External Affairs, Government of India.</p>
 
<p align="justify">She is one of the nodal officers for the Centre for Internal Quality Assurance of IGNOU. As a core team member, she designs curricula as part of expert committees of IGNOU’s academic programmes. Various other events organised by the School of Journalism require her to coordinate and be a part of the organizing teams in various capacities. National agencies invite her as an area expert for examination-related activities. She also serves as a member on the Board of Studies in different Schools of IGNOU and other Universities.</p>
 
<p align="justify">Prof. Rai has produced E-content for various platforms like writing and recording modules for E-PG Pathshala on ‘Media and Communication Studies’, a UGC sponsored E-learning initiative in collaboration with the Ministry of Education, GOI and Inflibnet. Further, she has contributed modules to MOOCs like Society and Media and Media, Information and Empowerment which are currently offered on SWAYAM. She lectures regularly on the Gyan Darshan TV channel and Gyan Vani radio as well as on the official Facebook page and YouTube channel of IGNOU. Her lectures are also available digitally through various online programmes and e- Gyankosh, the digital repository of IGNOU.</p>
 
<p align="justify">In the past, she coordinated the ‘Train the Trainer’ workshops for working journalists in collaboration with Deutsche Welle, Germany. She has scores of invited lectures to her credit for students and newly joined college and university teachers at educational and training institutions, not-for-profit organisations, HRDC of some universities and prestigious institutions like the Indian Institute of Mass Communication and National Institute of Fashion Technology in various areas of mass communication, train the trainer, communication skills and personality development. Her latest book is Films, Cinema and Movies: How Internet is Shaping the Entertainment Industry published by HP Hamilton, London.</p>

<p>Prof. (Dr.) Shikha Rai</br>
Director</br>
School of Journalism and New Media Studies</br>
